  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV and AIDS in Brazil: mapping and assessement of the current situation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2007, the BSCG team received funds from the programme development fund in order to establish a partnership with a new partner Pastoral da Aids, with a view to the setting up of a HIV and Aids programme in Brazil.  This new partnership was part of a strategy of redefining our work on HIV and Aids in Brazil. 
Parts of these funds approved were destined for activities related to programme set up.  The following approval is for these funds.  These activities were planned to include set up and monitoring visits and partner meetings with potential further partners.  In addition to this, in order to complement the work of Pastoral da Aids and strengthen CAFOD&#x2019;s contribution to working on HIV and AIDS in Brazil, we commissioned the translation of the HIV review document into English for use by CAFOD. We plan to produce a summary document to illustrate the case of HIV and AIDS in Brazil, in particular the role of advocacy.</narrative>
  </description>
